spans.s:
mā́s [397], m.
 —1. moon, see candra-mās;
then (as in Eng.), a moon, i. e. month.
[‘the measurer,’ √1mā, 1151. 1c^2: cf.
μή-νη, ‘moon’; Lat. Mēna, ‘menstruationis
dea’; Goth. mena, AS. mōna, Eng. moon;
AS. mōnan dæg, ‘dies Lunae,’ Eng. Monday;
also μήν, stem μενς, Lat. mens-i-s,
‘month’; AS. mōnað, prop. ‘a lunation,’
Eng. month.]
